{"title":"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A wire is cut into two pieces, one of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the other of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. The piece of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is bent to form an equilateral triangle, and the piece of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is bent to form a regular hexagon. The triangle and the hexagon have equal area. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad2a3d82ed49fca22d2128a1af4015408c5bb54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"410\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the area formulas for an equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b661fc4a2ac6f87e4fe1febf84514a81572b0231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{{s}^{2}\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"68\" height=\"53\" /> and regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff86b836cee7e367e117400760ed5338ee8be7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3{s}^{2}\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"77\" height=\"53\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11bf3a731f2a0ca35db4e686b6eef5a11dfa264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358a21468dc3aadff232bbcb3caa154fe807f446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> into each equation, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eafc7775bac37a248c8e004907faab18b840d9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{a}^{2}\\sqrt{3}}{36}=\\frac{{b}^{2}\\sqrt{3}}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"41\" />. Simplifying this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b314fa2c5224f4167ce3dc530f8a4cd54211287d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The regular hexagon can be broken into 6 small equilateral triangles, each of which is similar to the big equilateral triangle. The big triangle's area is 6 times the area of one of the little triangles. Therefore each side of the big triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af834b481b16223a0f04fa9a05f4f8a581e0182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> times the side of the small triangle. The desired ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f965e897b00fbf1db301ce4c610b40978846416a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{6}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\Rightarrow(B).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to avoid fractions we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd8b8ff0937e1a6d9fc9a5b0171ec89543dde85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc6eebb04dd3045115f5f65e401510966d092d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 6y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. Then we only need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a16f474c2f9c02c3b39ddd68e96851187b12c4b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x/y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" />. The side length of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and the side length of the hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55838a17c4f636ee7bc6391690e8895adb487e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2x)^2\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{3y^2\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"43\" />. Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05d0a32cf9b198758c36440c1dd867741976a38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{y^2} = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"44\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/053109d4b2e3f33094f72c543f62a5ae63a5b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />. Rationalizing the denominator, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6bd3869d9ec5d91139346dbf0d16bb52ab88c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{ (B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"72\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B\">2013 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017150427\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 221/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4664/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.853      1 -total\n 60.25%    7.744      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.69%    4.973      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11780:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017150427 and revision id 263800. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}